xt"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that reports each edge once, by its position, from the end that reaches it first. The tree","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge into a vertex is not reported again from it, so a parallel edge to the parent is a back","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge. It holds a copy of the graph and can be iterated more than once, and keeps its own stack.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"UndirectedEdgeDepthFirstSearch","kind":"symbol"}}}